    "articleNo": "6-1-4",
    "krTitle": "인접 공항 운영(Adjacent Airport Operation)",
    "krContent": "터미널(TERMINAL)\n항적난기류(Wake Turbulence) 적용\n인접 공항들에 대한 관제 관할권을 지닌 항공교통관제기관은 다음과 같은 기준에 따라\n항적난기류 분리를 요하는 항공기의 비행경로를 통과하게 될 진로 상에서 도착 또는\n출발하는 IFR 항공기를 분리하여야 한다.\n가. 초대형(super)항공기 뒤 대형(heavy), 중형 또는 소형항공기 − 3분\n나. 대형(heavy)항공기 뒤 대형(heavy), 중형 또는 소형항공기 − 2분\n다. B757 항공기 뒤 소형항공기 − 2분\n라. 항적난기류 그룹을 적용하는 경우\n1) 그룹 A 항공기 뒤 그룹 B, C, D, E, F, G 항공기 – 3분\n2) 그룹 B, C 항공기 뒤 그룹 B, C, D, E, F, G 항공기 − 2분\n그림 6-1-1 인접공항운영 - 도착\n그림 6-1-2 인접공항운영 - 출발",
    "faaTitle": "ADJACENT AIRPORT OPERATIONS",
    "faaContent": "TERMINAL No Change\nWAKE TURBULENCE APPLICATION No Change\nThe ATC facility having control jurisdiction at a. The ATC facility having control jurisdiction at\nadjacent airports must separate arriving or adjacent airports must separate arriving or\ndeparting IFR aircraft on a course that will cross the departing IFR aircraft on a course that will cross the\nflight path of an aircraft requiring wake turbulence flight path of an aircraft requiring wake turbulence\nseparation in accordance with the following: separation in accordance with the following:\na. Heavy, large, or small behind super − 3 minutes. 1. Category B, C, D, E, F, G, H, or I aircraft\nbehind Category A aircraft − 3 minutes.\nb. Heavy, large, or small behind heavy − 2 2. Category B, C, D, E, F, G, H, or I aircraft\nminutes. behind Category B or D aircraft − 2 minutes.\nAdd 3. Category E, F, G, H, or I aircraft behind\nCategory C aircraft − 2 minutes.\nc. Small behind B757 − 2 minutes. 4. Category I aircraft behind Category E\naircraft − 2 minutes.\nBriefing Guide BG−69\nAdd b. EN ROUTE. The ATC facility having control\njurisdiction at adjacent airports must separate\narriving or departing IFR aircraft on a course\nthat will cross the flight path of an aircraft\nrequiring wake turbulence separation in\naccordance with the following:\nAdd 1. Heavy, large, or small behind super − 3\nminutes.\nAdd 2. Heavy, large, or small behind heavy − 2\nminutes.\nAdd 3. Small behind B757 − 2 minutes.\nOLD NEW"
